IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `sda-home`

-- Stamp Duties Act 1923 (SA), with the Stamp Duties Regulations 2013 -- duty on an application to register a motor
-- vehicle or to transfer its registration. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own terms ("the applicant",
-- "the value of a motor vehicle"). The buyer's questions are in sda-seat.l4.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- through the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0). The Act's deposited text is AS AT 2025-02-13 (scraped
-- 2025-03-10); the Regulations' AS AT 2022-09-29 (scraped 2024-09-13), at
-- ../../../stamp-duties-regulations-2013/registers/source-bundle/stamp-duties-regulations-2013.txt. Not the official
-- texts; they may be out of date. The scale is encoded as the deposited text states it.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 42A (terms); s 42B(1) (value of a motor vehicle), (1a) (state the value, regulative), (1d) (the
-- registration component, plus the policy of insurance component on an application to register but not on a transfer),
-- (2) (paid to the Registrar at the time of making the application, regulative); s 42BA (a transfer of registration where
-- a registered owner continues: its formula is missing, so the answer is `not covered` unless an exemption leaves no
-- duty, s 42BA(2)); s 71CB(2)(a)(ii), (b), (3) (from sda-home.l4: a transfer between spouses or domestic partners,
-- current or former, applied first); Schedule 2 clause 2(1) (the registration component, as two tables, non-commercial and
-- commercial or trailer, with the $5 minimum); clause 2(2) exemptions 4 (a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle), 6 (ad
-- valorem duty already paid, to that extent) and 11 (an entitlement under Motor Vehicles Act 1959 s 38 to a reduced
-- registration fee, an INPUT); clause 2(3) (the policy of insurance component); clause 2(4) exemptions 2 (a trailer that
-- is not a heavy vehicle), 6 (s 38 reduced fee) and 8 (a State concession card of the class prescribed by Regulations
-- 2013 reg 14, or a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, with reduced public transport fares).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the s 42BA(1) amount itself (its formula is missing -- `not covered`); s 42B(1b), (1c) (the
-- Commissioner's valuation), (4)-(6) (an application not lodged as required); ss 42C, 42CA (refunds); the other clause
-- 2(2) and 2(4) exemptions (dealers, the Crown, councils, deceased estates, hire purchase, buses, disability, primary
-- producers, and the rest); Regulations 2013 regs 10A, 10B (heavy vehicles, electric vehicles).
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Stamp Duties Act 1923 -- duty on registering a motor vehicle, seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 42B(1) -- the value of a motor vehicle`

-- s 42B(1): "the value of a motor vehicle is -- (a) in the case of an application to register a new motor vehicle for
-- which there is a list price -- (i) if the motor vehicle has no optional equipment, the list price of the vehicle; or
-- (ii) if the motor vehicle has optional equipment, the list price of the motor vehicle plus the list price or, if there
-- is no list price, the actual price (inclusive of GST) of the equipment; or (b) in the case of an application to
-- transfer the registration of a second-hand motor vehicle upon sale of the vehicle, the consideration for the sale or
-- the market value of the motor vehicle, whichever is the higher; or (c) in any other case, the market value (inclusive
-- of GST) of the motor vehicle." s 42A: "list price" is "inclusive of GST"; "new motor vehicle means a motor vehicle not
-- previously registered in this State or elsewhere". (1a): the applicant "must state in the application the value";
-- (1b): the Commissioner may have it valued if not satisfied.
DECLARE `Kind of vehicle application` IS ONE OF
    `registering a new motor vehicle that has a list price`
    `transferring the registration of a second-hand motor vehicle on its sale`
    `any other application`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of vehicle application`
      `the list price of the vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `the list price, or else the actual price, of the optional equipment` IS A NUMBER
      `the consideration for the sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the market value, including GST` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the motor vehicle (s 42B(1))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `registering a new motor vehicle that has a list price` THEN
        `the list price of the vehicle` PLUS `the list price, or else the actual price, of the optional equipment`
    WHEN `transferring the registration of a second-hand motor vehicle on its sale` THEN
        `the greater of` `the consideration for the sale` `the market value, including GST`
    WHEN `any other application` THEN `the market value, including GST`

§§ `Schedule 2 clause 2(1) -- the registration component, as tables`

-- Schedule 2 clause 2(1): "Application to register or transfer the registration of a motor vehicle -- component payable
-- in respect of registration -- (a) where the value of the motor vehicle (not being a commercial motor vehicle or a
-- trailer) -- (i) does not exceed $1 000 -- for every $100 or fractional part of $100 of that value $1.00; (ii) exceeds
-- $1 000, but does not exceed $2 000: $10.00 plus $2.00 for every $100 or fractional part of $100 of the excess over
-- $1 000 of that value; (iii) exceeds $2 000, but does not exceed $3 000: $30.00 plus $3.00 ... over $2 000; (iv) exceeds
-- $3 000: $60.00 plus $4.00 ... over $3 000. (b) where the value of the motor vehicle (being a commercial motor vehicle or
-- a trailer) -- (i) does not exceed $1 000 -- ... $1.00; (ii) exceeds $1 000, but does not exceed $2 000: $10.00 plus
-- $2.00 ... over $1 000; (iii) exceeds $2 000: $30.00 plus $3.00 ... over $2 000. (c) if the application is not exempt
-- from duty but the amount of the duty would, apart from this paragraph, be less than $5, the component in respect of
-- registration is to be $5." "commercial motor vehicle" and "trailer" have the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 meanings (s 42A):
-- FACTS.
DECLARE `Vehicle band` HAS
    `above`       IS A NUMBER
    `base amount` IS A NUMBER
    `per 100`     IS A NUMBER

`the non-commercial vehicle table (clause 2(1)(a))` MEANS
    LIST `Vehicle band` OF 3000, 60, 4
         `Vehicle band` OF 2000, 30, 3
         `Vehicle band` OF 1000, 10, 2
         `Vehicle band` OF 0, 0, 1

`the commercial vehicle or trailer table (clause 2(1)(b))` MEANS
    LIST `Vehicle band` OF 2000, 30, 3
         `Vehicle band` OF 1000, 10, 2
         `Vehicle band` OF 0, 0, 1

GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `Vehicle band`
      `the value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount on the vehicle table` MEANS
    CONSIDER `table`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `band` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the value` GREATER THAN `band`'s `above`
        THEN `band`'s `base amount`
             PLUS (`band`'s `per 100` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the value` MINUS `band`'s `above`))
        ELSE `the amount on the vehicle table` `rest` `the value`

`the minimum registration component (clause 2(1)(c))` MEANS 5

GIVEN `the value of the motor vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration component before exemptions (clause 2(1))` MEANS
    `the greater of` `the scale amount` `the minimum registration component (clause 2(1)(c))`
    WHERE
        `the scale amount` MEANS
            IF `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer`
            THEN `the amount on the vehicle table` `the commercial vehicle or trailer table (clause 2(1)(b))` `the value of the motor vehicle`
            ELSE `the amount on the vehicle table` `the non-commercial vehicle table (clause 2(1)(a))` `the value of the motor vehicle`

§§ `Schedule 2 clause 2(2) -- exemptions from the registration component (4, 6 and 11)`

-- Exemption 4: "Any application to register or to transfer the registration of a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle."
-- Exemption 6: "Any application to register a motor vehicle or to transfer the registration of a motor vehicle to the
-- extent that ad valorem stamp duty has already been paid, or is payable, on another instrument by which or by virtue of
-- which the property in the motor vehicle was, or will be, legally or equitably transferred to, or vested in, the
-- applicant." Exemption 11: an application "in the name of a person who -- (a) is entitled under section 38 of the Motor
-- Vehicles Act 1959 to have the motor vehicle registered at a reduced registration fee; and (b) is not enjoying the
-- benefit of this exemption in respect of any other motor vehicle currently owned by the person." The s 38 entitlement
-- is a Motor Vehicles Act test, a FACT. READING (NOTES.md, finding 11): exemption 6 reduces the component by the ad
-- valorem duty paid; the $5 minimum of clause 2(1)(c) is applied before it, and a component wholly covered is nil.
DECLARE `Vehicle exemption facts` HAS
    `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `ad valorem duty paid or payable on another instrument transferring the vehicle`    IS A NUMBER
    `the applicant is entitled under MVA s 38 to a reduced registration fee`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant enjoys exemption 11 or policy exemption 6 for another vehicle owned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant owns the vehicle`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant holds a State concession card of the prescribed class`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant holds a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the card entitles the applicant to reduced public transport fares in the State`   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `e` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration component is wholly exempt (clause 2(2), exemptions 4 and 11)` IF
        `e`'s `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`
    OR  (    `e`'s `the applicant is entitled under MVA s 38 to a reduced registration fee`
         AND (NOT (`e`'s `the applicant enjoys exemption 11 or policy exemption 6 for another vehicle owned`)))

GIVEN `the value of the motor vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `e` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration component (clause 2(1), (2))` MEANS
    IF `the registration component is wholly exempt (clause 2(2), exemptions 4 and 11)` `e`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`the registration component before exemptions (clause 2(1))` `the value of the motor vehicle` `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` MINUS `e`'s `ad valorem duty paid or payable on another instrument transferring the vehicle`)

§§ `Schedule 2 clause 2(3), (4) -- the policy of insurance component`

-- s 42B(1d): "(a) payable upon an application to register a motor vehicle shall be an amount calculated by the addition
-- of -- (i) the amount prescribed by Schedule 2 as the component payable in respect of registration; and (ii) the amount
-- prescribed by Schedule 2 as the component payable in respect of a policy of insurance; or (b) payable upon an
-- application to transfer the registration of a motor vehicle shall be the amount prescribed by Schedule 2 as the
-- component payable in respect of registration and ... no additional component shall be payable in respect of a policy
-- of insurance." "policy of insurance means a policy of insurance under Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959" (s 42A):
-- compulsory third party insurance.
-- Clause 2(3): "where the application is for registration of the vehicle for a period of -- (aa) not more than 31 days
-- $5.00; (a) more than 31 days but less than 12 months (for each 3 months or part of each 3 months in the period of
-- registration) $15.00; (b) 12 months $60.00". A period longer than 12 months is not in the table: `not covered`.
DECLARE `Period of registration` IS ONE OF
    `not more than 31 days`
    `more than 31 days but less than 12 months` HAS `months, counting a part month as a month` IS A NUMBER
    `12 months`
    `more than 12 months`

GIVEN `the period` IS A `Period of registration`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the policy of insurance component before exemptions (clause 2(3))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `not more than 31 days` THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 5
    WHEN `more than 31 days but less than 12 months` `months` THEN
        `the amount, in dollars, is` (15 TIMES `the number of parts of` 3 `in` `months`)
    WHEN `12 months` THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 60
    WHEN `more than 12 months` THEN `not covered` `a registration period longer than 12 months is not in the Schedule 2 clause 2(3) table`

-- Clause 2(4) exemption 2: "Policy of insurance where the application is for registration of a trailer that is not a
-- heavy vehicle." Exemption 6: the applicant "(a) is entitled under section 38 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 to have the
-- motor vehicle registered at a reduced registration fee; and (b) is not enjoying the benefit of this exemption in respect
-- of any other motor vehicle currently owned by the person." Exemption 8: the applicant satisfies the Registrar "(a) that
-- he is the owner of the motor vehicle; (b) that he is entitled as the holder of -- (i) a State concession card of a
-- prescribed class; or (ii) a pensioner entitlement card issued under any Act or law of the Commonwealth, to travel on
-- public transport in this State at reduced fares." Regulations 2013 reg 14: "a State concession card issued by the
-- administrative unit that is, under a Minister, responsible for the administration of the Family and Community
-- Services Act 1972 is a State concession card of a prescribed class."
GIVEN `e` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy of insurance component is exempt (clause 2(4), exemptions 2, 6 and 8)` IF
        `e`'s `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`
    OR  (    `e`'s `the applicant is entitled under MVA s 38 to a reduced registration fee`
         AND (NOT (`e`'s `the applicant enjoys exemption 11 or policy exemption 6 for another vehicle owned`)))
    OR  (    `e`'s `the applicant owns the vehicle`
         AND (`e`'s `the applicant holds a State concession card of the prescribed class` OR `e`'s `the applicant holds a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card`)
         AND `e`'s `the card entitles the applicant to reduced public transport fares in the State`)

§§ `s 42B(1d) -- the duty on the application`

GIVEN `it is an application to register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the motor vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period` IS A `Period of registration`
      `e` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty on the vehicle application (s 42B(1d))` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is an application to register`)
    THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` `registration`
    ELSE IF `the policy of insurance component is exempt (clause 2(4), exemptions 2, 6 and 8)` `e`
         THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` `registration`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the policy of insurance component before exemptions (clause 2(3))` `the period`
              WHEN `the amount, in dollars, is` `policy` THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` (`registration` PLUS `policy`)
              WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHERE
        `registration` MEANS `the registration component (clause 2(1), (2))` `the value of the motor vehicle` `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` `e`

§§ `s 42BA -- a transfer of registration where a registered owner continues`

-- s 42BA(1): "The amount of duty payable on an application to transfer the registration of a motor vehicle where a
-- person who is a registered owner of the motor vehicle immediately before the registration is transferred will
-- continue to be a registered owner of the motor vehicle immediately after the registration is transferred is
-- calculated as follows: [formula missing from the deposit] where -- D is the amount of duty payable; A is the amount of
-- duty that would be payable apart from this section; B is the number of persons that the application seeks to add to,
-- or remove from, the register as owners ..., whichever is the greater; C is ... the number of persons who are registered
-- owners ... immediately before ... or ... immediately after ..., whichever is the greater." (2): "This section does not
-- derogate from any other provision conferring an exemption under this Act." (3): it "applies to applications executed
-- after its commencement". The formula (stamp-duties-act-1923.formulas.md, line 624) is not in the deposit and is not
-- guessed: a continuing-owner transfer answers `not covered`. READING (NOTES.md, finding 22): where the clause 2(2)
-- exemptions leave no registration component (A is nil), s 42BA(2) keeps that exemption whole, so the answer is nil.
-- Adding or removing a co-owner (one owner staying on) is the usual case.
GIVEN `it is an application to register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a registered owner immediately before the transfer will continue to be one immediately after it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the motor vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period` IS A `Period of registration`
      `e` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty on the vehicle application (ss 42B(1d), 42BA)` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `it is an application to register`)
       AND `a registered owner immediately before the transfer will continue to be one immediately after it`
    THEN IF `the registration component (clause 2(1), (2))` `the value of the motor vehicle` `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` `e` EQUALS 0
         THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
         ELSE `not covered` `the s 42BA formula for a transfer of registration to or from a continuing owner is missing from the deposited text`
    ELSE `the duty on the vehicle application (s 42B(1d))` `it is an application to register` `the value of the motor vehicle` `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` `the period` `e`

§§ `s 71CB(2)(a)(ii), (b) with ss 42B and 42BA -- the duty on a vehicle application`

-- s 71CB(2): "an instrument of which the sole effect is -- (a) to transfer -- ... (ii) registration of a motor vehicle,
-- between parties who are spouses or former spouses, or domestic partners or former domestic partners; or (b) to
-- register a motor vehicle in the name of a person whose spouse or former spouse, or domestic partner or former domestic
-- partner, was the last registered owner of the vehicle ..., is exempt from stamp duty", between former partners only if
-- the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown (s 71CB(3), a fact). An application is an
-- instrument chargeable under Schedule 2 clause 2 (s 42A(2) for an electronic one). The exemption applies first; s 42BA(2) keeps it whole for a continuing
-- owner. Otherwise the duty is s 42B(1d), or s 42BA for a continuing owner.
GIVEN `its sole effect is to transfer the registration between the parties, or to register it in the name of the last owner's partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship` IS A `Relationship of the parties`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an application to register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a registered owner immediately before the transfer will continue to be one immediately after it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the motor vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period` IS A `Period of registration`
      `e` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty on the vehicle application (ss 42B, 42BA, 71CB)` MEANS
    IF `the vehicle application is exempt (s 71CB(2)(a)(ii), (b))` `its sole effect is to transfer the registration between the parties, or to register it in the name of the last owner's partner` `the relationship` `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown`
    THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
    ELSE `the duty on the vehicle application (ss 42B(1d), 42BA)` `it is an application to register` `a registered owner immediately before the transfer will continue to be one immediately after it` `the value of the motor vehicle` `it is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer` `the period` `e`

§§ `s 42B(1a), (2) -- state the value and pay the duty with the application (regulative)`

-- s 42B(1a): "An applicant for registration, or transfer of registration, of a motor vehicle must state in the
-- application the value of the motor vehicle as at the date of the application." (2): "The amount payable upon an
-- application in accordance with subsection (1d) shall be paid by the applicant to the Registrar of Motor Vehicles at
-- the time of making the application." Clock: days from making the application, so both are due on day 0. s 42D applies
-- the Taxation Administration Act to duty paid to the Registrar "as if the Registrar were the Commissioner", so unpaid
-- duty is a tax default (TAA s 3), with interest under Part 5 Division 1. An application with no duty payable (exempt,
-- or wholly covered) has no payment to make; the value must still be stated.
`the days to pay the duty on a vehicle application (s 42B(2))` MEANS 0

GIVEN `duty is payable on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 42B(1a), (2) -- state the value and pay the duty to the Registrar when applying` IS
    IF `duty is payable on the application`
    THEN    (PARTY  `the applicant for registration or transfer of registration of a motor vehicle`
             MUST   `state the value of the motor vehicle in the application`
             WITHIN `the days to pay the duty on a vehicle application (s 42B(2))`
             LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant for registration or transfer of registration of a motor vehicle` BECAUSE "s 42B(1a): the application must state the value of the motor vehicle as at the date of the application")
        RAND
            (PARTY  `the applicant for registration or transfer of registration of a motor vehicle`
             MUST   `pay the duty to the Registrar of Motor Vehicles`
             WITHIN `the days to pay the duty on a vehicle application (s 42B(2))`
             HENCE  FULFILLED
             LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant for registration or transfer of registration of a motor vehicle` BECAUSE "s 42B(2): the duty must be paid to the Registrar of Motor Vehicles at the time of making the application; unpaid, it is a tax default under the Taxation Administration Act 1996 (s 42D), with interest from the end of the last day for payment (TAA s 25)")
    ELSE    PARTY  `the applicant for registration or transfer of registration of a motor vehicle`
            MUST   `state the value of the motor vehicle in the application`
            WITHIN `the days to pay the duty on a vehicle application (s 42B(2))`
            LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant for registration or transfer of registration of a motor vehicle` BECAUSE "s 42B(1a): the application must state the value of the motor vehicle as at the date of the application"
